{"name":"Rockabilly","hex":"#6c7186","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rockabilly","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A genre of music originating from the South (United States) and mixing elements of rock, blues, country, hillbilly boogie and bluegrass music.","A member of the subculture associated with rockabilly music."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rockabilly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rockabilly","blocks":[{"text":"Rockabilly is one of the earliest styles of rock and roll music. It dates back to the early 1950s in the United States, especially the South. As a genre, it blends the sound of country and western music with that of rhythm and blues, leading to what is considered \"classic\" rock and roll. Some have also described it as a blend of bluegrass with rock and roll. The term \"rockabilly\" itself is a portmanteau of \"rock\" and \"hillbilly\", the latter a reference to the country music that contributed strongly to the style. Other important influences on rockabilly include Western swing, boogie-woogie, jump blues, and electric blues."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/GazzguzzlersAtCaddysDiner.jpg/330px-GazzguzzlersAtCaddysDiner.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockabilly","wikidata":"Q203720"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Elvis_Presley_promoting_Jailhouse_Rock.jpg/500px-Elvis_Presley_promoting_Jailhouse_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Elvis_Presley_promoting_Jailhouse_Rock.jpg/1280px-Elvis_Presley_promoting_Jailhouse_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Elvis_Presley_promoting_Jailhouse_Rock.jpg/500px-Elvis_Presley_promoting_Jailhouse_Rock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Elvis Presley in a promotional shot for Jailhouse Rock in 1957","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElvis_Presley_promoting_Jailhouse_Rock.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/BillHaley.JPG/500px-BillHaley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/BillHaley.JPG/1280px-BillHaley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/BillHaley.JPG/500px-BillHaley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bill Haley and His Comets during a TV appearance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABillHaley.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Teddy-et-the-Tigers-1978.jpg/500px-Teddy-et-the-Tigers-1978.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Teddy-et-the-Tigers-1978.jpg/1280px-Teddy-et-the-Tigers-1978.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Teddy-et-the-Tigers-1978.jpg/500px-Teddy-et-the-Tigers-1978.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Teddy & The Tigers, a Finnish rockabilly band from Kerava, pictured in Helsinki, 1978","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATeddy-et-the-Tigers-1978.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}